<title>USA: Pittsburgh faces $4.5 mln budget shortfall.</title>
<headline>Pittsburgh faces $4.5 mln budget shortfall.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pittsburgh is facing a $4.5 million budget shortfall after city officials neglected to allocate funds for two arbitration rulings.</p>
<p>The money was needed to pay city firefighters and to settle a Justice Department consent decree ruling.</p>
<p>Mayor Tom Murphy said money put aside for future projects would be used to make up the difference.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
